  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $7?$\n\nI. $448$\n\nII. $352$\n\nIII. $217$",
  "worked_solution": "To check if a number is divisible by $7,$ double the last digit, subtract the result from the remaining digits, and then check if the difference is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $448,$ we have that \n\n$$\n44-2(8)=44-16=28\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $448$ is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $352,$ we have that \n\n$$\n35-2(2)=35-4=31\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $352$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $217,$ we have that \n\n$$\n21-2(7)=21-14=7\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $217$ is divisible by $7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
